---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
const plausible = Boolean(
  import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN &&
  import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_SCRIPT_URL,
);
const umami =
  !plausible &&
  Boolean(
    import.meta.env.PUBLIC_UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID &&
    import.meta.env.PUBLIC_UMAMI_SCRIPT_URL,
  );
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How reading, search, newsletter subscriptions, optional analytics, and external media handle information on this website."
>
  <div class="container narrow section" data-legal-review="pending">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Your privacy</p><h1>Room to read quietly.</h1><p>
        Last updated 6 November 2026.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="callout">
        Draft privacy notice — human and legal review is pending. The owner must
        confirm the responsible legal entity, privacy contact, hosting provider,
        retention periods, and any configured services before public launch.
        This draft does not establish that those checks have happened.
      </p>
      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is an educational website. The person or organization responsible
        for personal information, sometimes called the data controller, has not yet
        supplied its legal name or privacy contact. <a href="/contact/"
          >Contact availability</a
        > shows the current status. Do not send private health information or identity
        documents through an unverified contact route.
      </p>
      <h2>Reading and searching</h2>
      <p>
        You do not need an account to read. There are no comments, reader
        profiles, or forms for health stories. Search runs in your browser using
        a downloaded Pagefind index. Search words are not sent to an outside
        search provider. Your browser may keep a page or search history
        according to your own settings.
      </p>
      <h2>Hosting and technical information</h2>
      <p>
        The host may process your IP address, requested page, request time, and
        browser information to deliver and protect the website. These details
        can reveal what you read. The owner must confirm the host, purposes,
        access controls, retention period, and deletion arrangements, and
        publish those details before launch.
      </p>
      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      {
        plausible || umami ? (
          <p>
            This build has {plausible ? 'Plausible' : 'Umami'} analytics
            configured. The intended setup measures general use without
            advertising cookies. The owner must confirm the actual data
            collected, provider, lawful basis, storage location, retention, and
            any consent or opt-out requirements. “Cookieless” does not mean that
            no personal information can be processed.
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>
            This build has no analytics script configured. The website's own
            reading and search features do not set advertising or tracking
            cookies. The owner must separately confirm the hosting and access
            service's handling of technical information.
          </p>
        )
      }
      <h2>Newsletter subscriptions</h2>
      {
        site.newsletter.action ? (
          <p>
            A newsletter form is active in this build. It sends your email
            address directly to the configured outside provider. The owner must
            add that provider's name and privacy terms, confirm any technical
            information it collects, and verify its confirmation and unsubscribe
            flows before public launch. The intended setup requires a
            confirmation email before subscription.
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>
            Newsletter signup is not active in this build. There is no
            newsletter form collecting your address. If enabled later, the form
            will send your email directly to the chosen provider, with
            provider-side confirmation before subscription.
          </p>
        )
      }
      <p>
        A newsletter address should be used only for the purposes explained at
        signup. You can withdraw permission for future emails by using the
        unsubscribe link in an issue. The owner must confirm the provider's
        retention and deletion process. Do not put health information in signup
        fields.
      </p>
      <h2>Other websites and media</h2>
      <p>
        Reference links and support directories lead to other services with
        their own privacy practices. An enabled YouTube player connects to
        youtube-nocookie.com only after you choose to load it. YouTube can then
        receive technical information about your visit and apply its own terms.
        Choosing a podcast platform also takes you to an outside service.
      </p>
      <h2>Purposes, legal grounds, and retention</h2>
      <p>
        The intended purposes are delivering the site, protecting its operation,
        providing a requested newsletter, and measuring broad use only when
        analytics are enabled. Where a law requires a legal ground for
        processing, the owner must document it for each purpose. This may
        include consent for a newsletter or a properly assessed legitimate
        interest for necessary operations; this draft does not select a ground
        on the owner's behalf.
      </p>
      <p>
        Keep information only as long as needed for the stated purpose or a
        legal duty. Specific periods for hosting logs, newsletter records, and
        analytics are not yet confirmed. Service providers, processing
        locations, and any safeguards for transfers between countries must also
        be identified before launch.
      </p>
      <h2>Rights in the European Economic Area and United Kingdom</h2>
      <p>
        Where the GDPR or a similar law applies, you may be able to ask for
        access to your information, correction of errors, deletion, limits on
        use, or a portable copy. You may also object to some uses, withdraw
        consent where processing relies on it, or complain to your local data
        protection authority. These rights depend on the circumstances and can
        have legal exceptions. Withdrawing consent does not undo earlier lawful
        processing.
      </p>
      <h2>Rights for California residents</h2>
      <p>
        If the California Consumer Privacy Act applies to the operator and your
        information, rights can include knowing and accessing information
        collected, correcting it, deleting it, and opting out of a sale or
        sharing covered by that law. Limits on certain uses of sensitive
        personal information may also apply. A covered business must not
        discriminate against someone for using these rights.
      </p>
      <p>
        The planned site has no advertising system or mechanism for selling
        reader information. The owner must verify the actual practices of all
        configured services, whether the law applies, and any required opt-out
        or browser preference handling. Do not treat this draft as a completed
        California privacy disclosure.
      </p>
      <h2>Making a privacy request</h2>
      <p>
        A working privacy contact and a secure request process are still
        required. Once available, explain what you are requesting and the
        service involved. The owner may need proportionate proof of identity
        and, where applicable, authorization for an agent. Do not send sensitive
        documents unless a verified, secure process specifically needs them.
        Requests must be handled within applicable legal time limits, subject to
        permitted exceptions.
      </p>
      <h2>Security and changes</h2>
      <p>
        No website can promise perfect security. The owner must review provider
        access, HTTPS, retention, and incident handling. This notice needs a new
        review when the site operator, services, data uses, or legal
        requirements change. The date above identifies this draft, not legal
        approval.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
